From 28a00a76531e7c6b83bc5cc4517d553fcbfbb935 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajhochy <ajhochy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 01:11:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] feat(desktop): supervise Open Design runtime
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Slice 1 of the Open Design integration: checksum-pinned runtime staging
plus a pure/testable resolver and lifecycle supervisor. No /design UI,
webview, preload bridge, or theme injection yet (later slices).

- electron/open-design/manifest.ts: parses the frozen contract's pinned
  tag/commit/license/per-platform SHA-256 assets into a validated manifest.
- electron/open-design/namespace.ts: deterministic, traversal-safe,
  Windows-path-budget-bounded namespace derivation from a Hermes profile
  name, plus the Hermes-owned profile-scoped runtime path tree.
- electron/open-design/identity.ts: structural validation of Open Design's
  on-disk web-root.json identity and a strict loopback-http URL check.
- electron/open-design/resolver.ts: packaged-then-installed precedence,
  requiring an exact 0.20.0 match on both paths so an incompatible
  installed runtime (e.g. 0.18.1) is never silently accepted.
- electron/open-design/state.ts: the renderer-safe state allowlist —
  strips executable paths, argv, env, child pid, and log content.
- electron/open-design/child-env.ts: allowlisted child environment
  builder — forwards HERMES_BIN and OD_* vars, never provider secrets.
- electron/open-design/readiness.ts: bounded readiness probe combining
  identity validation with a loopback HTTP health check.
- electron/open-design/supervisor.ts: concurrency-safe, idempotent
  OpenDesignRuntimeSupervisor — attach-vs-owned tracking, bounded
  crash-loop retry, graceful-then-forced stopOwned, and no child leak on
  a stop-during-start race.
- scripts/open-design/stage.mjs: staging CLI — resolves platform/arch,
  downloads the pinned GitHub release asset, verifies SHA-256 before
  extraction (fails closed on mismatch), extracts via hdiutil
  (always detaches) on macOS or 7-Zip on Windows (clear error if absent),
  and is deterministic no-op on Linux. Stages Resources + upstream
  Apache-2.0 LICENSE + a provenance manifest. Installer downloads and
  staged output live outside Git (OS cache dir + gitignored build/).
- New `test:open-design` / `stage:open-design` npm scripts.

Verified with a live isolated headless spike against the installed
(incompatible, 0.18.1) Open Design.app in a disposable namespace/root:
confirmed the `main.cjs --headless` + OD_PACKAGED_CONFIG_PATH launch form,
the exact web-root.json identity shape, the /api/health and /api/version
responses, graceful SIGTERM teardown of the whole sidecar tree, and no
process/root residue afterward. The 0.20.0 production compatibility
policy in resolver.ts is unchanged by this — the spike only proves launch
mechanics.

