From 4359c7b7ebfd1de1508a561383fc46296986c7ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajhochy <ajhochy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 01:55:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] fix(desktop): harden Open Design runtime integration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Repairs the three rejected P0s (supervisor spawned HERMES_BIN instead of
the resolved candidate; macOS staging dropped everything but Resources;
electron-builder never packaged the staged runtime) plus the P1s: unify
resolver/supervisor candidate types, forward HERMES_HOME, and make the
spawn assertion in tests actually check command/args instead of a fake
that ignored them.

Also hardens staging (checksum-valid cache reuse, atomic .part downloads,
path-traversal rejection, stage-then-atomic-publish, ditto-based full .app
copy — including a real mount-point parsing bug found by the live DMG
proof), generates a minimal no-telemetry OD_PACKAGED_CONFIG_PATH at mode
0600, tightens the child env allowlist, makes a stale-PID identity file
transient instead of fatal, replaces raw error strings with static
renderer-safe error codes plus a state subscription hook, adds bounded
crash-restart to the supervisor, and wires electron-builder's mac
extraResources to the staged runtime.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
