From: ajhochy <ajhochy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 12:58:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] fix(desktop): repair Open Design Windows Job guardian and
 close S1 review findings

Repairs the FAIL/REJECT verdict on cc201d895 (0 P0, 4 P1, 4 P2, 1 P3) and
completes the partial Windows Job guardian work in progress:

- P1-1: supervisor.ts already modeled async spawn errors correctly; verified
  and added an idempotent concurrent-stopOwned() regression.
- P1-2: Windows headless identity/readiness cross-check (headless-root.json +
  desktop IPC status + strict health) was implemented; added missing
  drive-letter/space/non-ASCII fixtures and fixed a resolver.ts discriminated-
  union narrowing bug (`'reason' in closure`, not `!closure.ok`, under this
  tsconfig's relaxed strictNullChecks) that silently broke typecheck.
- P1-3: rewrote the ODJOB/1 protocol to the full
  `READY <guardianPid> <guardianCreationFiletime> <targetPid> <targetCreationFiletime> <sourceCommit> <nonce>`
  handshake in both guardian.cpp and the TS adapter; replaced the adapter's
  two-competing-stdout-listener state machine with one bounded parser;
  switched termination detection from 'exit' to 'close' so a final buffered
  EMPTY can never race a false ownership_lost; fixed ForceEmptyJob() to never
  report EMPTY without proving ActiveProcesses==0; made malformed/oversized
  control input fail closed (force cleanup) instead of report-and-continue;
  bound the guardian's target to argv (no more spawning with zero args);
  added guardian PID/nonce validation and target creation-FILETIME binding to
  the graceful-stop IPC leg; require shutdown `accepted:true` before trusting
  it. Implemented `stageWindowsJobGuardianForPack` (real build-on-Windows and
  fail-closed supplied-artifact paths) and wired it into before-pack.mjs +
  package.json's win.extraResources. Added a windows-latest CI job that
  compiles the guardian and runs the desktop suite on a real Windows host.
- P1-4, P2-1..P2-4, P3: HERMES_BIN resolution, native runtime closure
  validation, immutable keyed publication, canonical packaged-config,
  bounded download, and fatal-catalog live smoke were already complete;
  verified with a real mac-arm64 signed-app run (checksum, signature, 88 live
  models, graceful IPC shutdown, zero residual processes) and a real staged
  resource audit for both mac-arm64 and win32-x64 payloads.

Unverified (no Windows host available): real MSVC compilation, actual Job
Object lifecycle/crash behavior, PE signing, and installed NSIS/MSI smoke.
These remain the mandatory pre-production gate on real Windows CI.

