+ * always big-endian on disk regardless of host byte order, which is what
+ * every real Xcode/lipo-produced universal binary uses). Returns `null` for
+ * anything that is not a recognized thin 64-bit or fat Mach-O -- the caller
+ * must treat `null` as "cannot prove architecture", never as an
+ * empty-but-valid slice list.
