 ## Product flow
 
@@ -65,6 +65,8 @@ Hermes /design ─start─► │ OpenDesignRuntimeSupervisor │
 
 Packaged builds stream the official platform release asset into an external checksum cache, verify SHA-256 before extraction, and atomically stage the complete signed macOS app or the recursively merged Windows NSIS app payload. `electron-builder` includes that platform-specific payload with its license and exact provenance. Installer/runtime binaries never enter Git; Linux deterministically skips bundled staging.
 
+The original OD-02 assumption — that the Open Design Resources tree alone could be launched by pointing the packaged Hermes executable at its `app/main.cjs` — was falsified against the packaged Hermes executable (a renamed packaged Electron binary ignores an alternate `main.cjs` app path and boots its own embedded Hermes application), and the release payload contains no plain-Node headless bundle to fall back to. [Amendment 1](./open-design-integration.amendment-1.json) records that evidence, the resulting decision to stage and launch the complete signed official application instead, the size impact, and the rejected sidecar-reimplementation alternative; the acceptance behavior of OD-02 through OD-13 is unchanged.
